.TH SPACES 8 "2026-09-26" "storage-spaces 0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
spaces \- read Microsoft Storage Spaces pools on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spaces scan
.br
.B spaces attach
.RB [ \-\-pool
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-space
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR auto | dm | ublk | nbd | fuse ]
.RB [ \-\-degraded ]
.RI [ device ...]
.br
.B spaces detach
.RI [ space ]
.br
.B spaces status
.br
.B spaces info
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.IR device ...
.br
.B spaces extents
.I device ...
.B \-\-space
.I name
.br
.B spaces export
.I device ...
.B \-\-space
.I name
.B \-\-output
.I file
.br
.B spaces dm\-table
.I device ...
.B \-\-space
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spaces
reads the metadata of Microsoft Storage Spaces pools (Windows 10 and 11
layout) from their member disks and exposes the virtual disks ("spaces") as
read-only Linux block devices. It never writes to pool members.
.PP
Supported: simple, two- and three-way mirror, single and dual parity spaces,
storage tiers,
fixed and thin provisioning, the per-space write-back cache, pools with
missing or failing disks as far as the redundancy allows. Not supported yet:
writing, pool management, pools created by other Windows releases.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Lists the Storage Spaces pool members found among the block devices, grouped
by pool, with the spaces of each pool.
.TP
.B attach
Attaches the spaces of every complete pool (or of the selected pool/space).
Each space appears as
.BI /dev/mapper/ss\- pool \- space
and every partition inside it as
.BI /dev/mapper/ss\- pool \- space \-p N\fR.
Pools with missing disks are skipped unless
.B \-\-degraded
is given. Spaces already attached are left alone.
.TP
.B detach
Removes the devices of the given space (name, GUID or device-mapper name) or
of all attached spaces, and stops their serving processes.
.TP
.B status
Lists attached spaces, their backends and partition devices.
.TP
.B info\fR, \fBextents\fR, \fBexport\fR, \fBdm\-table
Inspect a pool given by its member devices or images: pool, disks and
spaces; the slab allocation of a space; copy a space into a sparse image
file; print a device-mapper table for a simple or mirror space.
.SH BACKENDS
.TP
.B dm
Device-mapper table over the member devices; no process. Used by
.B auto
for simple spaces whose logical sector size matches the members'.
.TP
.B ublk
A
.B spaces serve\-ublk
process (transient systemd unit) behind
.BR /dev/ublkb N;
needs Linux 6.0 or newer and the
.B ublk_drv
module. Exposes the space's own sector size and keeps reading when a mirror
copy or parity column fails.
.TP
.B nbd
A
.B spaces serve\-nbd
process connected with
.BR nbd\-client (8).
.TP
.B fuse
A
.B spaces serve\-fuse
process exposing an image file, attached with
.BR losetup (8).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/storage-spaces/
State of attached spaces.
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/69-storage-spaces.rules
Starts
.B storage-spaces-attach.service
when a pool member appears.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
spaces scan
spaces attach
mount \-o ro /dev/mapper/ss\-Storage_pool\-Data\-p2 /mnt
spaces detach
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmsetup (8),
.BR nbd\-client (8),
.BR losetup (8),
.BR mount (8)
